# WT-3-prod-multidevice — Cloud sandbox device template.
#
# This device runs slave-C on a single cloud droplet, providing the
# cross-internet tunnel path that host-mode / same-LAN configs cannot
# exercise. Default vendor is DigitalOcean; alt vendors ∈ {e2b, vps}.
#
# HARNESS-ONLY: oauth_placeholder MUST stay literal. The `vendor:`
# line is single-key (spec §7(h)) — change one line to switch vendor.
# NO real droplet is created by this worktree; cloud_up.sh + teardown.sh
# only print `doctl` / `e2b` / `ssh` commands they would run.

kind: device
role: slave-c
device_kind: cloud
listen: 127.0.0.1:18093
oauth_placeholder: <OAUTH_TOKEN_HERE_DO_NOT_COMMIT>
vendor: digitalocean
notes: |
  Default vendor = digitalocean (single droplet). Change `vendor:` to
  `e2b` or `vps` to switch. Vendor-conditional commands:
    - digitalocean → doctl compute droplet create / delete
    - e2b          → e2b sandbox create / delete
    - vps          → ssh <user>@<host> systemctl start/stop loom-slave
  See wrappers/cloud_up.sh for print-only invocation.
